From b0d2c2b462e07bf7f3f4b2e47ed0169e2ac22d97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:55:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-234: FFT waves and ripple strength on the Vulkan
 Cata water (no water shader change)

- The Cata water pixel shaders derive normals from one-texel height differences of the ripple maps (s4/s8). A new
  composite pass (CataRippleWaves.frag) writes two maps the water samples instead: 128 yd = Cata ripples x strength +
  ship hulls + FFT waves (full to 40 yd, fading by 58 yd); 512 yd = waves alone (to 205-246 yd). Heights from the same
  CPU FFT as D3D9 (HD::WaterWavesSample, device-free), Hermite-interpolated from the FFT slopes, scaled so the normal
  tilt equals the wave slope; spectrum from the nearest Cata water's Forever liquid type.
- hdWaterWaves / hdWaterWaveScale / hdWaterRipples / hdWaterRippleStrength now work on Vulkan; waves off and strength
  1 = the old path at no cost. hdCataWaterInfo reports ripples and waves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
